# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sched-2 window (the admission levers; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sched-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-2 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-sched-2/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the
# same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone.
# A1 (EXACTNESS with seed first and the hold's reading reuse on, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-s5-audit, the ship-5 audited twin (every audit of
# the candidate) with the two levers of docs/tp4-sched2.md that touch the order of work on, on Swift: the seed token leaves the engine before the request's engine is bound
# (the bind runs at the start of the next scheduling call, ahead of the scheduler's own clock, hold and gate), and the DRAM hold reuses a recent allocator reading while it
# clears the terms. Neither changes what a round computes: the order of the device work, the scheduler's view and the pacing are the eager order's; the audits (the rebind's
# digests against a cold twin, the carry, the K/V page writer, the tier) run over every admission. Tests: warmup; coding (one user); concurrent8_drain (eight users whose
# budgets end one by one: every live count from 8 to 1, so every hold and every bind happens beside every number of decoders); concurrent8_steady (eight fresh prompts
# together into a process whose slots are new: eight deferred binds in a row, the hold reuse at its limit); agent_turns (the returning turns that reach the rebind and the
# exact resume). READ: c2_smoke_check clean; every audit line exact=True with entries above 0. LEVERS: the lines each lever logs (a lever whose line is absent did not
# engage, and its arm reads NOT_EXERCISED): "[PINDIAG] admission pipeline installed: seed_first=.. hold_reuse=.. ledger_trim=.." once; SEED FIRST: "[PINDIAG] admission seed
# first deferred request=.. slot=.." and "[PINDIAG] admission seed first built request=.. ms=.. after_seed_ms=.." per deferred admission (after_seed_ms is how long the
# first token left ahead of the bind), "[PINDIAG] admission seed first eager request=.. reason=.." for each bind that stayed in the sampler; HOLD REUSE: "[PINDIAG]
# admission hold reading reused prompt=.. age_ms=.. reuses=.." per reused hold (the dram admission fit lines then number the real readings); LEDGER TRIM: "[PINDIAG]
# admission ledger trim: the memory ledger ended after the attach" once and no "memory_ledger_before" line with "op": "rebind" in the whole log EXACT READ: every user's
# answer is byte-identical to the control's (the same checkpoint, greedy: a difference is a token a lever changed and is NO-GO); no "audit mismatch", no "fell back", no
# "admission seed first: the bind of" error line (a refusal after a seed had gone: it stops the engine, and the preflight makes it unexpected), no engine death, no stall.
# CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models
# answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through
# the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the
# lever. Duration (estimate): 80 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-s5-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
